{
  "dom_id": "step-e5634",
  "name": "Example: Computing a Probability Involving Mutually Exclusive Events",
  "problem": "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events. Given that $P(A)=\\dfrac{1}{3}$ and $P(A\\cup B) = \\dfrac{4}{9},$ find $P(B).$",
  "worked_solution": "If $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events, then $P(A\\cap B) = 0.$ \n\nTherefore, by the addition law, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B) \\\\ P(B) & =P(A\\cup B)-P(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-3}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
